  content: `
  <p>Renting a car for the first time can seem confusing. You may have questions about insurance, deposits, fuel, mileage, documents, and what happens when you return the vehicle.</p>

  <p>The good news is that the process becomes much easier once you know what to check before booking.</p>

  <p>Here are eight simple steps to help you rent a car confidently and avoid unexpected costs.</p>

  <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1549317661-bd32c8ce0db2?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80" alt="Car available for rental during a trip" class="in-article-img" />

  <h2>🚗 Choose the Right Car for Your Trip</h2>

  <p>Start by thinking about what you actually need from the rental car.</p>

  <p>A small car can be practical for city driving and may be easier to park, while a larger vehicle can make sense for families, groups, or trips involving substantial luggage.</p>

  <p>Do not automatically choose the largest or cheapest vehicle. Consider the number of passengers, luggage space, driving conditions, and type of trip.</p>

  <h2>💰 Compare the Total Rental Price</h2>

  <p>The advertised rental price is not always the final amount you will pay.</p>

  <p>Check whether the quote includes taxes, fees, mileage, insurance options, additional drivers, and other charges.</p>

  <p>A car with a slightly higher daily rate may actually be cheaper overall if it includes services that another rental charges separately.</p>

  <p>Always compare the complete price rather than focusing only on the daily rate.</p>

  <h2>📄 Check the Documents You Need</h2>

  <p>Rental requirements can vary depending on the country, rental company, vehicle, and driver's circumstances.</p>

  <p>Before booking, check which documents are required. These may include a valid driving licence, identification or passport, booking confirmation, and an accepted payment card.</p>

  <p>If you are renting abroad, also check whether an international driving permit or other documentation is required for your destination.</p>

  <h2>🛡️ Understand the Insurance</h2>

  <p>Insurance is one of the most important things to understand before collecting your rental car.</p>

  <p>Do not assume that the cheapest rental automatically provides the level of protection you need.</p>

  <p>Read what is covered, what the excess or deductible may be, and whether exclusions apply.</p>

  <p>If you already have coverage through another provider, check its terms carefully before deciding whether additional rental protection is necessary.</p>

  <h2>💳 Know About the Deposit</h2>

  <p>Many rental companies place a temporary authorization or hold on your payment card when you collect the vehicle.</p>

  <p>The amount can depend on the vehicle, rental company, location, and protection selected.</p>

  <p>Before booking, check how much money may need to be available on your card and how the deposit or authorization works.</p>

  <p>This can help prevent an unpleasant surprise at the rental desk.</p>

  <h2>⛽ Check the Fuel Policy</h2>

  <p>Fuel policies can differ between rental companies.</p>

  <p>A common arrangement is to collect the car with a full tank and return it full, but other policies may apply.</p>

  <p>Read the fuel terms before accepting the vehicle and keep your fuel receipt when appropriate.</p>

  <p>Returning the car with less fuel than required can result in additional charges.</p>

  <h2>📸 Inspect the Car Before Driving Away</h2>

  <p>Before leaving the rental location, walk around the vehicle and check its condition.</p>

  <p>Look for scratches, dents, damaged wheels, cracked glass, or other visible issues.</p>

  <p>Make sure existing damage is recorded according to the rental company's process. Taking clear photographs or video can also help you keep a record of the vehicle's condition at pickup.</p>

  <blockquote class="editorial-quote">
    "Before driving away, make sure you know what you are paying for and that the car's existing condition has been properly recorded."
  </blockquote>

  <h2>🗺️ Understand the Driving Rules</h2>

  <p>If you are renting a car in another country, take a few minutes to understand the local driving rules.</p>

  <p>Check which side of the road people drive on, local speed limits, parking rules, toll systems, road signs, and any restrictions that may affect your journey.</p>

  <p>If you are unfamiliar with the destination, download offline maps or make sure you have reliable navigation available before starting your trip.</p>

  <h2>🧳 First-Time Car Rental Checklist</h2>

  <div class="flight-tips-card">
    <h3>🚗 Before You Book</h3>

    <p><strong>Car:</strong> Choose a vehicle that fits your passengers, luggage, and trip.</p>

    <p><strong>Price:</strong> Compare the complete rental cost, not only the daily rate.</p>

    <p><strong>Documents:</strong> Confirm the driving licence, identification, and payment requirements.</p>

    <p><strong>Insurance:</strong> Understand coverage, exclusions, and any excess or deductible.</p>

    <p><strong>Deposit:</strong> Check how much may be held on your payment card.</p>

    <p><strong>Fuel:</strong> Read the fuel policy before collecting the car.</p>

    <p><strong>Condition:</strong> Document existing damage before driving away.</p>

    <p><strong>Return:</strong> Check the return location, opening hours, fuel requirements, and late-return rules.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>🔑 Don't Forget the Return Process</h2>

  <p>Returning the car is just as important as collecting it.</p>

  <p>Check the return instructions before your rental ends. Confirm the location, opening hours, fuel requirements, mileage limits, and whether after-hours returns are allowed.</p>

  <p>Give yourself enough time to return the vehicle without rushing.</p>

  <p>Keep your rental agreement and any relevant receipts until the final charges have been settled.</p>

  <h2>✈️ Compare Car Rentals With FlySava</h2>

  <p>Renting a car for the first time becomes much easier when you know what to check before booking.</p>

  <p>Compare the total price, vehicle type, insurance, deposit, fuel policy, mileage, pickup location, and return conditions before making your choice.</p>

  <p><strong>FlySava</strong> helps you plan more of your trip in one place, including flights, hotels, car rentals, flight status, eSIM options, and destination travel information.</p>

  <div class="flight-tips-card">
    <h3>🧳 Before Picking Up Your Rental</h3>

    <p><strong>Confirm:</strong> Your booking, pickup time, and location.</p>
    <p><strong>Bring:</strong> All required documents and an accepted payment method.</p>
    <p><strong>Review:</strong> Insurance and deposit requirements.</p>
    <p><strong>Inspect:</strong> The vehicle and record existing damage.</p>
    <p><strong>Check:</strong> Fuel, mileage, and return conditions.</p>
    <p><strong>Drive:</strong> Follow local traffic and parking rules.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <details class="faq-accordion">
    <summary>What do I need to rent a car for the first time?</summary>
    <p>Requirements vary by country and rental company, but you will generally need a valid driving licence, identification, booking details, and an accepted payment method. Check the specific requirements before your trip.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="faq-accordion">
    <summary>Is rental car insurance necessary?</summary>
    <p>Insurance requirements and available protection vary by location and rental company. Read the coverage, exclusions, and excess carefully and check whether you already have applicable coverage elsewhere.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="faq-accordion">
    <summary>Why do car rental companies require a deposit?</summary>
    <p>A rental company may place a temporary authorization or hold on your payment card as security for potential charges. The amount and conditions vary by company, location, and vehicle.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="faq-accordion">
    <summary>What should I check when picking up a rental car?</summary>
    <p>Check the vehicle for existing scratches, dents, damaged wheels, cracked glass, and other visible issues. Make sure existing damage is recorded and keep your own photographs or video as a record.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="faq-accordion">
    <summary>What is the best fuel policy for a rental car?</summary>
    <p>Policies vary, but a full-to-full arrangement can be straightforward because you collect the vehicle with a full tank and return it full. Always check the specific rental agreement.</p>
  </details>

  <details class="faq-accordion">
    <summary>What should I check before returning a rental car?</summary>
    <p>Check the return location and opening hours, fuel requirements, mileage conditions, and after-hours instructions. Allow enough time to return the vehicle and keep relevant receipts and documents.</p>
  </details>

  <h2>Final Thoughts</h2>

  <p>Renting a car for the first time does not need to be complicated.</p>

  <p>Choose the right vehicle, compare the complete price, understand insurance and deposits, check the fuel policy, inspect the car, and learn the return requirements before you drive away.</p>

  <p>A few minutes of preparation can help you avoid unexpected charges and make your trip much smoother.</p>

  <p><strong>Compare car rental options with FlySava and plan the rest of your journey with flights, hotels, and other travel services in one place.</strong></p>
`
